Year = {2001},
Volume = {16},
Pages = {197-202},
Note = {10th Bethel Cleveland-Clinic Symposium, BIELEFELD, GERMANY, APR, 1999},
Abstract = {Eight times per year the specialized epilepsy centre the `Dr. Hans
   Berger Clinic', in Breda, the Netherlands, offers the Five-Day Epilepsy
   Programme (FEP). The FEP is a multidisciplinary, diagnostically
   comprehensive, psychoeducative programme, designed for six people with
   epilepsy and their partners being admitted as inpatients from Monday to
   Friday to a separate unit of the clinic. Evaluative research indicates
   that, after participation in the FEP, people with epilepsy and their
   partners are far better informed about epilepsy and better able to cope
   with it. Partly as a consequence of this, they exhibit a reduction in
   feelings of anxiety and stress.
   The FEP is suitable for people whose epilepsy has only recently been
   diagnosed, those who require a second professional opinion and those who
   are experiencing concomitant problems of whatever nature.},
