   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {In this paper, the characteristics and formation of engineering
   geological environment and the important effect of regional tectonic
   movement on them in the Chengdu area are discussed; the main
   environmental engineering geological problems-the quality of subgrade,
   the conditions of foundation pit construction, the harmfulness of
   earthquake and the situation of groundwater as an additional resource
   for supply are obtained through analysis; a series of factors which
   these problems depend on are studied. Conforming to principle of
   systematic analysis and applying different mathematical methods (such as
   multivariable regression analysis, decision matrix, synthetical fuzzy
   judgement and so forth), they are evaluated in regular sequence.
   Finally, the quality of the engineering geological environment of the
   Chengdu proper is graded comprehensively according to appraisal results
   of single factor, and the direction favourable to urban construction
   development of Chengdu City is suggested.},
