Abstract = {The article deals with the development of height growth of underplanting
   depending on uper storey stocking on top parts of the Ore Mountains.
   These plantations grew up at the turn of 70's and 80's of the last
   century as a substitute for air pollution damaged autochthonous stand.
   Original, mainly beech spruce stands were cut down on more than 40000
   hectares for reason that majority of tree species dieback because of
   high emission load. The deforestation of tracts mainly touched the
   plateaus of the Ore Mountains. European larch, blue spruce and pine
   exotics, white birch, mountain ash, speckled alder and green alder were
   used as. These stands substitute refforestation tree species are
   intensively recovered with original tree species, especially with common
   spruce. The three regeneration methods used in this are: regeneration
   under native stand, regeneration by border felling and regeneration on
   clearcut area. The increment depends on the degree of weed infestation
   and stocking above all. Spruce is planting under stand shutter. The
   maximal value of increment is 12.61 cm while the stocking is 0.9. The
   spruce outplaning made on border felling area with width 4 metres has
   the highest value of increment of 12.52 cm while outplaning on clearcut
