Abstract = {There were 69 invasive and potentially invasive species in the flora of
   Sterlitamak in the Bashkortostan Republic (Russia). Eight are in the
   most dangerous types of invasive species. The greatest danger is
   represented by: Acer negundo, Ambrosia trifida, Elodea canadensis and
   Xanthium albinum. Within the boundaries of Sterlitamak, 21 syntaxa (13
   associations and 8 derivated communities) are invasive species. This
   phytocenosis in an urban environment can be prime targets for plant
   quarantine actions.},
