   ALBUQUERQUE, NM, NOV 09-13, 1996},
Organization = {Soc Amer Foresters},
Abstract = {This study assessed the nontimber benefits of the forest stands
   resulting from four different site preparation methods in the Tuskegee
   National Forest by using the Contingent Valuation Method. Results
   indicated that the public demanded the National Forest to be managed for
   both timber and nontimber product, and that for nontimber benefits they
   seemed to prefer the forest stand without site preparation than those
   treated with chainsaw felling, tree injection, and soil-active herbicide
