   Transportat; Minist Hlth; Minist Environm},
Abstract = {The aim of the paper is to introduce the reader to the international
   project ``Transportation, Air Pollution, and Physical Activities: an
   integrated health risk assessment programme of climate change and urban
   policies (TAPAS){''} and to compare characteristics of the case study
   areas analyzed under the project. The purpose of the TAPAS is to help
   decision makers design urban policies through assessing and quantifying
   impacts of these policies on health and climate change. Under the
   project, a concept of integrated health risk assessment will be used and
   a quantitative model, which will be calibrated on data of the six case
   study areas (Barcelona, Paris, Basel, Copenhagen, Warsaw, and Prague),
   will be developed.},
