Note = {4th International Conference on Emotions and Organizational Life,
   Birkbeck Coll, London, ENGLAND, JUN, 2004},
Abstract = {This article uses a social constructionist approach based on ethnography
   and narrative analysis to understand emotions in leadership. The
   empirical context of the study is leadership of a theater ensemble's
   rehearsal process. The study shows that a creative process, such as in a
   theatrical setting, involves emotional paradoxes. Specifically, the
   study points out how shame can be used as a leadership tool to increase
   organizational performance and professional development, rather than for
   purposes of manipulation as may be typically assumed.},
